    "alert_id": "EX4_001",
    "title": "Carbamazepine contraindicated with DTG",
    "message": "Guidelines list carbamazepine as a contraindication for DTG, and note that carbamazepine decreases DTG levels by 30–70%, recommending use of valproic acid instead. The patient was started on carbamazepine 2 weeks ago while already on DTG. The viral load has risen from <50 to 1,240 copies/mL despite reported good adherence, consistent with reduced DTG exposure. The patient is already on sodium valproate, which the guidelines specifically recommend as the alternative antiepileptic.",
    "issue_type": "drug_interaction",
    "severity": "critical",
    "recommended_action": "Stop carbamazepine and manage seizures with valproic acid as guidelines recommend. Repeat viral load after adjustment and assess for resistance if viremia persists.",
