    "alert_id": "EX4_002",
    "title": "Carbamazepine toxicity with elevated level",
    "message": "The patient has a carbamazepine level of 14 mcg/mL (therapeutic 4–12), with symptoms of ataxia, nystagmus, tremor, dizziness, and headache. Hyponatraemia (Na 128 mmol/L) is also consistent with carbamazepine toxicity. The clinician plans to reduce the dose and repeat the level. However, given the DTG interaction and guideline contraindication, discontinuation rather than dose reduction is warranted. ALT 68 U/L may also reflect carbamazepine hepatotoxicity, though valproate is another potential cause.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Discontinue carbamazepine entirely rather than dose-reducing, given the DTG contraindication. Monitor sodium and ALT until normal. Use valproate for seizure management.",
