    ]
  },
  {
    "alert_id": "EX4_003",
    "title": "Detectable viral load requires adherence support",
    "message": "Guidelines state that virological monitoring detects treatment failure early and indicates need to switch therapy to reduce resistance accumulation. The viral load rose from <50 to 1,240 copies/mL within 6 months. While the DTG–carbamazepine interaction is the likely cause of reduced DTG levels, the plan does not address adherence counselling or a repeat viral load after correcting the interaction. Early repeat VL testing is needed to confirm whether viremia resolves once DTG levels are restored.",
    "issue_type": "plan_add",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "After stopping carbamazepine, repeat viral load in 2–3 months. Provide enhanced adherence support. If still detectable, proceed to genotype testing per guidelines.",
